 * Freescale MC13783/MC13892 Power Management Integrated Circuit (PMIC)
 
 Required properties:
-- compatible : Should be "fsl,mc13783" or "fsl,mc13892"
+- compatible : Should be "fsl,mc13783" or "fsl,mc13892". Kindle K4/Yoshi
+  may use "amazon,kindle-k4-mc13892", "fsl,mc13892" to select single-word
+  32-bit SPI frames required by its i.MX50 CSPI controller.
 
 Optional properties:
 - fsl,mc13xxx-uses-adc : Indicate the ADC is being used
 - fsl,mc13xxx-uses-codec : Indicate the Audio Codec is being used
 - fsl,mc13xxx-uses-rtc : Indicate the RTC is being used
 - fsl,mc13xxx-uses-touch : Indicate the touchscreen controller is being used
+
+Kindle K4 charger sub-node (local port only):
+- charger: A child of the K4 PMIC with compatible =
+  "amazon,kindle-k4-mc13892-charger". The MFD attaches this node to the
+  charging policy device. status = "disabled" suppresses this child.
+  The charger starts in observation mode; a node does not authorize writes.
+  Put the following properties on this child, so an unavailable fuel gauge
+  or detector defers the charging consumer without deferring the PMIC's
+  regulators, RTC and power button. Keep fsl,mc13xxx-uses-adc on the PMIC.
+  Earlier experimental trees with amazon,charger-policy and flat parent
+  properties remain supported, but retain their parent-level dependencies.
+- amazon,battery-supply : Phandle to the K4 ti,bq27210 fuel gauge. Required
+  on the charger child; used for power_supply data and read-only pack
+  ID / fresh temperature reads at fixed K4 gauge registers.
+- amazon,usb-budget-supply : Phandle to amazon,k4-usb-phy, providing the
+  gadget current budget. Required on the charger child.
+  Use fsl,mc13xxx-uses-adc as well for the input-voltage measurement path.
+- amazon,charger-detect-supply : Optional phandle to the MAX14656 detector.
+  Its fresh CURRENT_MAX advertises autonomous source permission (zero for
+  SDP); the policy takes the larger of this and the gadget budget. Read
+  failures stop the charge decision. Board/current/thermal/ADC guards still
+  apply. Omission retains gadget-only behavior. A device link orders PM.
+- amazon,max-charge-current-microamp : Optional board ceiling, 80000 (default)
+  through 1600000, rounded down to an MC13892 table 63 regulated DAC setting.
+  The initial software limit remains 80000; userspace must explicitly take
+  control. Source budget and temperature may reduce the selected current.
+  Code 15 is an unregulated external-supply mode and is never selected.
+- amazon,usb-current-reserve-microamp : Allowance outside the regulated
+  charge path, including USB PHY, indicator and board tolerance. Default
+  60000: table 64's 440 mA upper bound for the recommended 400 mA USB DAC
+  setting leaves 60 mA within a 500 mA source budget. This is a board policy
+  allowance, not a measurement of actual input current. The selector uses
+  table 64's upper current bound plus this allowance; insufficient budget
+  stops charging. Verify the allowance against the actual board and load.
+
+- Optional amazon,charge-led-triggers on the charger enables k4-charge-active
+  and k4-charge-full triggers from the charger driver. Bind the GPIO charging
+  gate and MC13892 LED ID 6 to active, and the board's green LEDKP to full.
+  Requires CONFIG_CHARGER_K4_MC13892_LEDS; does not opt into current control.
+
+Example K4 charging consumer (phandles refer to board devices):
+  charger {
+    compatible = "amazon,kindle-k4-mc13892-charger";
+    amazon,battery-supply = <&battery_gauge>;
+    amazon,usb-budget-supply = <&usbphy0>;
+    amazon,charger-detect-supply = <&charger_detector>;
+    amazon,max-charge-current-microamp = <480000>;
+    amazon,usb-current-reserve-microamp = <60000>;
+  };
 
 Sub-nodes:
 - codec: Contain the Audio Codec node.
